# Third-party environment art, imported locally, NEVER committed.
#
# Content/CityPark/ is the Fab "City Park Environment Collection" (~1.5 GB), copied in from a
# local install of that pack -- see docs/citypark-level.md. It is licensed to Mike's Epic
# account, not to this repo: the Fab EULA grants use in projects, not redistribution of the raw
# assets, and this repo is PUBLIC. Committing it would be both a 1.5 GB binary blob in a repo
# whose rule is "never check binaries into git" and a licence breach. Anyone cloning this repo
# re-imports it themselves from their own Fab library.
#
# The level that USES it (Content/Maps/OB_City.umap) is small and IS committed -- it will show
# as a load error with unresolved references until the pack is imported, which is the intended
# and honest failure mode.
Content/CityPark/

# Content/Mannequins/ is Epic's template mannequin content (SKM_Manny_Simple + its skeleton,
# materials, textures and animations), shipped locally with every UE 5.7 install under
# Engine/../Templates/TemplateResources/High/Characters/Content/Mannequins/ -- see
# docs/mannequin-rider.md. It is licensed under the UE EULA as template content, not licensed for
# redistribution in an arbitrary public repo, and this repo is public: same reasoning as
# Content/CityPark/ above, not re-litigated here. ~126 MB, also fails the "never check binaries
# into git" rule on size alone. `ABoardActor`'s rider component (bShowRider) falls back
# gracefully -- board still renders, no rider, logged loudly -- if this directory is absent.
Content/Mannequins/

# macOS Finder noise.
.DS_Store
